324:- behavior-replay gate
362:### 10.3 Guide-reflection benchmark loop
366:- generate benchmark questions that test decision-quality answerability, not mere keyword presence
369:- patch the highest-signal gaps first, then rerun the same benchmark set instead of silently swapping questions
380:- document-benchmark to assembled-replay escalation
384:- for `runtime owner integrity`, document-level benchmark is sufficient when the reviewed runtime surfaces directly expose the owner boundary and no required behavior depends only on operator-facing prose
385:- for `benchmark-loop adequacy`, document-level benchmark is sufficient when the reviewed runtime surfaces directly expose the question -> answer -> verification -> rerun loop and explicit stop rule
386:- escalate those families to replay only when the claim is no longer about document/runtime parity and now depends on assembled behavior or actual runner execution state
389:- `Benchmark registry memo` for chapter-family inventory and expected verdict surface
390:- `Guide reflection benchmark memo` for question / answer / comparison / rerun tracking
392:- `Packet compliance report` when packet-floor doctrine is part of the failure surface
395:- if the live question has shifted from document reflection to assembled prompt behavior, escalate from `Guide reflection benchmark memo` to `Benchmark cohort manifest`
396:- if replay has actually been attempted, preserve `Replay runner verdict sheet` rather than prose-only replay status
397:- if multiple replayed scenarios must be summarized into one decision, preserve `Replay suite verdict memo` and keep partial coverage explicit
467:Prefer linked operational artifacts such as `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Release promotion decision record`, and `Telemetry drift investigation memo` when the gate depends on repeated execution evidence.
468:Keep `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` stable across benchmark, replay, release, and telemetry gates.
469:If the required packet floor is missing or joined artifacts fail precedence, compatibility, freshness, or completeness checks, downgrade the gate and keep `false-promotion`, `false-hold`, and `drift-triggered review` separate.
